cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Eulerian Video Magnification on CUDA"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite both this
  implementation and the original method it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kucuk
    given-names: Furkan
repository-code: "https://github.com/iamkucuk/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda"
url: "https://iamkucuk.github.io/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda/"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of Eulerian Video Magnification that amplifies colour and
  motion changes in video too small to see. Includes a NumPy implementation
  checked against the original authors' published output, a hand-written CUDA
  version for NVIDIA hardware, and a portable OpenCL version for Apple, AMD and
  Intel hardware, each compared against the NumPy reference by an automated
  test suite.
keywords:
  - eulerian video magnification
  - motion magnification
  - video processing
  - computer vision
license: LicenseRef-BSD-3-Clause-NonCommercial
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Eulerian Video Magnification for Revealing Subtle Changes in the World
    authors:
